/*
 * mxFiberCheck (MOXA-FIBER-CHECK-MIB, .1.3.6.1.4.1.8691.603.5.3)
 *
 * Second group migrated off the dlmod path, transcribed from
 * plugin_moxa_fiber_check/snmp/plugin_snmp_fiber_check.c. Two per-port
 * index-tables, no scalars:
 *
 *   .1 fiberCheckConfigPortTable   config layer, 9 columns, RW
 *   .2 fiberCheckStatPortTable     status layer, 13 columns, RO
 *
 * Both index columns (.1.1 and .2.1) are declared read-only in the MIB but the
 * dlmod never returned them, so a walk saw 20 of the MIB's 22 accessible
 * objects. The framework's index-table support returns them, so this migration
 * closes that gap: expect 22 columns, not 20.
 *
 * Six columns are not plain leaves and carry a suffix in uri_index telling
 * mapping_reuse.c which extraction to use (array_variant_col()):
 *
 *   "<field>[0]"  low end of a 2-element string array
 *   "<field>[1]"  high end of the same array
 *   "<field>[]"   the whole array rendered "[<low>, <high>]"
 *   "<field>[!]"  no backing field; GET is always TruthValue false(2)
 *
 * The pair columns share one config field, so the suffix — not the field name —
 * is what distinguishes them. Extraction and the whole-row SET live in
 * lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs/src/fiber_check.c, ported from the plugin.
 *
 * The status table needs the status layer rather than the config layer; the
 * setup fn in ies_auto_mibs_setup_net_mxFiberCheck.c sets
 * IES_FLAG_SNMP_URI_STATUS on those entries (same mechanism as mx_deviceIO).
 *
 * No IES_FLAG_SNMP_URI_INTERFACE anywhere here: that flag adjusts a port-index
 * *value* read out of config, whereas this table's 0-based/1-based row shift is
 * already done by the index-table path builder ("<uri><row-1>/<column>").
 */

